      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Self-treating a severe back injury with intense stretches or attempts to \"pop\" it is extremely dangerous and could permanently damage your nerves. A sudden \"pop\" with shooting leg weakness is a classic sign of a herniated disc pressing on a nerve root, which requires an MRI or CT scan to evaluate safely. Waiting for a doctor allows you to avoid long-term paralysis or chronic pain that likely won't resolve with home exercises. Please prioritize getting professional care immediately to protect your long-term mobility.",
      "source": "target",
